    "https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/pqoN7/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer-in-Agribusiness-HZAU-,2026-26079.html": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Agribusiness (HZAU)",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Agribusiness (HZAU) -\r\n        Lincoln University Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search careers@lincoln.ac.nz Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Agribusiness (HZAU) Teach and research in agribusiness and agricultural economics, supervise postgraduate students, and contribute to offshore teaching in China. Mō te tūka | The role Based in our Department of Agribusiness and Markets, you'll balance teaching, research, postgraduate supervision, and industry engagement while contributing to one of Australasia's leading agribusiness education and research environments. This role teaches across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, including the Bachelor of Agribusiness and Food Marketing and Master of Management (Agribusiness), while also supporting Lincoln University's partnership with Huazhong Agricultural University through offshore teaching in China. You'll have the opportunity to develop your research profile, supervise Masters and PhD students, and contribute to innovative teaching and learning practices. Some tasks of the role include: Deliver engaging undergraduate and postgraduate teaching Supervise Honours, Masters and PhD research students Develop and publish high-quality research outputs Contribute to curriculum and course development Foster partnerships with industry and external stakeholders Support offshore teaching delivery in China This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to a globally connected academic community while helping shape the future of agribusiness education and research. Mahi & Wāhi / Utu | Work pattern, location & salary This permanent role is based at our Lincoln Campus and works 37.5 hours per week (1.0 FTE), commencing 1 March 2027. As part of Lincoln University's partnership with Huazhong Agricultural University, the role includes offshore teaching in China for up to 16 weeks per year, delivered across four-week teaching blocks aligned with the academic calendar. The salary range for the role is Lecturer: Grade A6, $88,217 - $100,740 Senior Lecturer: Grade A7, $108,229 – $120,862 Kā tino Pūkeka/Whēako | Essential skills/experience for the role To be successful in the role you will have A PhD in agribusiness, agricultural economics, farm business management, or a related discipline A developing record of research and scholarly publication Experience teaching successfully in a tertiary education environment Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills The ability to build positive relationships with diverse students, colleagues and stakeholders A commitment to innovation in teaching, research, and student success, including the use of technology to enhance learning Availability to travel to China for up to 16 weeks per year Kā hua ka riro ki a koe | What's in it for you? Join a supportive, inclusive community that values diversity, wellbeing, and professional growth. Benefits include: Flexible, family‑friendly work + free on‑site parking Professional development & mentorship to grow your career Generous leave entitlements – six weeks of paid leave per year (based on 1.0 FTE) Annual salary reviews to recognise your contribution Contributions toward eye tests and prescription eyewear Free, confidential wellbeing support through Clearhead (EAP) Southern Cross employee benefits Access to on‑campus gym with discounted membership On‑site early childhood centre with staff discounts A vibrant campus lifestyle with cafés, green spaces, and a sense of community Mō mātou | About us Te Whare Wānaka o Aoraki | Lincoln University is a specialist institution dedicated to impactful research and higher education that supports land-based industries in New Zealand and globally. Our campus sits at the heart of the Lincoln research precinct, complemented by university-owned farms and research stations that blend education, research, and hands-on learning. At Lincoln, students are at the heart of everything we do, empower them to grow their potential and contribute to a more sustainably productive world through world-class teaching and research. As a progressive university with an ambitious vision, we value a professional workforce that reflects the diversity of our community. Our staff engage with students, parents, government, iwi, and external stakeholders, upholding Lincoln University’s reputation through their work. Our Te Tiriti o Waitangi commitments begin with mana whenua. We honour our special relationship with Ngāi Te Ruahikihiki and Te Taumutu Rūnanga, embedded in our He Tūtohinga Whakamātau | Charter of Understanding. Tono ināianei | Apply now Ready to apply? Submit your CV and a cover letter that highlights your fit - tell us why you want this role and what motivates you to join Lincoln University. Applications received via email will not be considered, however specific enquiry relating to the role can be made to david.dean@lincoln.ac.nz We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community where everyone feels valued and supported, and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. View the position description at: https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz Job Details Reference # 2026-26079 Posted on 02 Nov 2026 Closes on 22 Nov 2026 18:00 NZST Location(s) Lincoln University Campus Expertise Academic Work type(s) Permanent full-time More details (document) PD L-SL Agribusiness HZAU November 2026.pdf Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Back © Lincoln University Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 13 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance."
